Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(ArgWrite);
define
    awCaller=7;
    awOther=7;
    awHolder;
    awLeaf=99;
    awRead code={ return argument; };
    awWrite code={ argument = 5; return argument; };
    awRun code={
        r1 = awRead(awCaller);
        print "R1 read through the argument      " r1 " (want 7)":;
        awWrite(awCaller);
        print "R2 caller after write through arg " awCaller " (want 5 -- REFERENCE)":;
        print "R3 untouched sibling              " awOther " (want 7 -- ANTI-VACUITY)":;
        awHolder := awLeaf;
        r4 = awRead(awHolder);
        print "R4 read a GROUP-carrying caller   " r4 " (want 99)":;
        };
    ;
awRun();
print "ARGWRITE SENTINEL -- reached the foot":;
stop();

argWriteT -- DOES A WRITE THROUGH AN ARGUMENT REACH THE CALLER'S FIELD.
Minted 2026-08-30, and it is a PRE-FLIP instrument: it exists to be green NOW so
that it can go red if the wrapper flip breaks the thing the flip is meant to
preserve.

WHY IT EXISTS. The bind-by-body ruling stamped "actions mutate their caller's
field through the argument" as an eyes-open CONSEQUENCE of the flip. Filming the
wrapper on 2026-08-30 showed it is not a consequence at all -- IT IS ALREADY
TRUE. R2 reads 5 today. So the flip's job here is PRESERVATION, and the fleet
had no row that would notice if preservation failed.

⚠ AND THE MECHANISM THAT DELIVERS IT TODAY IS THE MECHANISM BEING REMOVED.
Plain `=` carries no `assign` flag (incant/setup), so runOP's `!op.isAssign` arm
is TRUE and the target IS unwrapped to the caller. Today the AUTO-UNWRAP is what
makes the wrapper transparent. Retire the unwrap without the wrapper and
`argument = 5` starts writing the wrapper instead of the caller -- no error, no
crash, no K-row motion, just a write that stops arriving. That is bear-trap #35's
class and it is the single hardest escape in the migration to see.

THE ROWS
  R1  a plain read through the argument reaches the caller's value      7
  R2  A WRITE through the argument REACHES THE CALLER'S FIELD           5
  R3  a sibling the action never touched is UNMOVED                     7
      ANTI-VACUITY: without it, a run where every field reads 5 -- or
      where writes leak everywhere -- would pass R2 and mean nothing.
  R4  the same read against a GROUP-carrying caller                     99
      pairs with R1 so the two data kinds are covered by one file, which
      is what "uniform, no data-keyed arm" has to mean in practice.

NEXT: RULED

Nothing here is owed a fix -- every row is green and is meant to stay green. The
ruling this file serves is the wrapper flip: ruleArg.group = argument, the four
unwrap lines and the && !arg.isArgument exemptions retire in ONE stroke. This
file is one of that stroke's certifications, pre-registered in
docs/wrapperPlan.md section 4. If R2 goes red on the flip, the two-half law was
violated -- half the stroke landed.
